===Level 98-99: Smithing Rune Equipment===
{{plinkp|{{MaxPrice|var=item|Rune 2h sword|Rune platelegs|Rune plateskirt|format=item|link=n}}}} Using a [[dwarven stout]], players can boost from 98 to 99 Smithing and smith [[rune platelegs]], [[rune plateskirt]]s, and [[rune 2h sword]]s as a [[Money_making_guide/Smithing_rune_items|potentially profitable]] alternative to adamant/rune platebodies. One [[dwarven stout]] must be drank every minute to maintain 99 Smithing from 98; this adds a cost of approximately one [[dwarven stout]] per 45 [[runite bars]], or roughly {{Coins|{{GEP|Dwarven stout}} / 45}} per bar.

Currently, the most profitable 3 bar rune item to smith when selling on the [[Grand Exchange]] is [[{{#var:item_item}}]]. If casting High Level Alchemy after smithing, it does not matter whether [[rune platelegs]], [[rune plateskirt]]s, or [[rune 2h sword]]s are made in terms of returns, as they have the same High Level Alchemy value; however, [[rune 2h sword]]s are the lightest and thus are slightly more efficient on run energy.

Experience rates of approximately 215,000 Smithing experience per hour can be obtained from equipment made with 3 [[runite bar]]s.

* Starting experience: 11,805,787.5
* Experience required: 1,228,643.5
* [[Runite bar]]s required: 16,383
* Most profitable: [[{{#var:item_item}}]]
* Input cost (bars and stouts): {{Coins|{{GEP|Runite bar|16383}} + ({{GEP|Dwarven stout}} * (16383/45))}}
* Output: {{Coins|{{GEP|{{#var:item_item}}|5461}}}}
* Profit: {{Coins|{{GEP|{{#var:item_item}}|5461}} - {{GEP|Runite bar|16383}} - ({{GEP|Dwarven stout}} * (16383/45))}} ({{Coins|{{GEP|{{#var:item_item}}}} - {{GEP|Runite bar|3}} - ({{GEP|Dwarven stout}} * (3/45))}} each)
* High alchemy ({{SCP|Magic|55}}) profit: {{Coins|({{HA|{{#var:item_item}}}}*5461) - {{GEP|Runite bar|16383}} - {{GEP|Nature rune|5461}} - ({{GEP|Dwarven stout}} * (16383/45))}} ({{Coins|{{HA|{{#var:item_item}}}} - {{GEP|Runite bar|3}} - {{GEP|Nature rune}} - ({{GEP|Dwarven stout}} * (3/45))}} each)

== AFK Methods ==

=== Level 1-99: Smelting Bars ===
As stated at the start of this guide, if you are just looking to make money or train smithing as fast as possible, it is usually better to train smithing using the faster methods above and use the time saved on faster money makers. However, smelting bars can be a good method for players looking for an AFK method that also generates a profit. Be sure to check the GE before making any bars to make sure you will be making a profit instead of a loss. To use this method, it is recommended that you bank a large number of ores ahead of time: either by purchasing them from the GE, or mining them yourself if you don't have any gold or want the mining experience. Then head to the [[Edgeville furnace|Edgeville Furnace]] as it is the closest furnace to a bank in free-to-play.

